WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.901 --> 00:00:03.203
-President Trump admitted
on Sunday

00:00:03.203 --> 00:00:05.938
that his campaign tried
to collude with Russia,

00:00:05.938 --> 00:00:07.373
capping off a busy weekend

00:00:07.373 --> 00:00:08.808
of tweeting
and watching cable news.

00:00:08.808 --> 00:00:11.177
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:13.179 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:15.315 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.315 --> 00:00:17.283
Donald Trump loves doing
three things --

00:00:17.283 --> 00:00:19.786
golfing, campaigning,
and watching TV.

00:00:19.786 --> 00:00:22.688
He's our first
retiree president.

00:00:22.688 --> 00:00:23.923
Pretty soon, he's going to put

00:00:23.923 --> 00:00:25.625
a retractable awning
on the White House

00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:27.727
and sit out there
with a word-search puzzle

00:00:27.727 --> 00:00:29.429
in his shorts and black socks.

00:00:29.429 --> 00:00:30.663
[ Laughter ]

00:00:30.663 --> 00:00:32.232
And this weekend,
Trump did all three

00:00:32.232 --> 00:00:33.666
of his favorite activities.

00:00:33.666 --> 00:00:35.935
On Friday night, he was at his
golf course in New Jersey

00:00:35.935 --> 00:00:38.203
when he went on Twitter
to attack LeBron James

00:00:38.203 --> 00:00:39.472
and CNN anchor Don Lemon.

00:00:39.472 --> 00:00:41.874
Now remember,
Trump has repeatedly insisted

00:00:41.874 --> 00:00:45.144
that he never watches CNN
while simultaneously complaining

00:00:45.144 --> 00:00:47.847
about what he sees
while watching CNN.

00:00:47.847 --> 00:00:51.284
-You look at, like, CNN, they'll
have a council of seven people.

00:00:51.284 --> 00:00:53.886
And of the seven people,
every one of them is against me.

00:00:53.886 --> 00:00:56.422
I'm saying where do they
even find these people?

00:00:56.422 --> 00:00:58.758
-I'm not your doctor,
Mr. President, but I would --

00:00:58.758 --> 00:01:01.027
I would recommend you watch
less of them.

00:01:01.027 --> 00:01:02.928
-I don't watch them at all.

00:01:02.928 --> 00:01:03.930
-Oh.

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:05.698
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.698 --> 00:01:08.467
That's like me saying
I don't watch "Real Housewives"

00:01:08.467 --> 00:01:10.470
but Dorinda better watch out!

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:12.772
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.772 --> 00:01:15.441
Well, apparently, Trump decided
to tune in Friday night

00:01:15.441 --> 00:01:17.376
when CNN aired an interview
with LeBron

00:01:17.376 --> 00:01:20.746
about a new public school
LeBron opened for at-risk youth.

00:01:20.746 --> 00:01:22.648
Lemon asked him
if he'd ever meet with Trump,

00:01:22.648 --> 00:01:23.950
and LeBron said this.

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:25.351
-What would you say
to the president

00:01:25.351 --> 00:01:26.418
if he was sitting right here?

00:01:26.418 --> 00:01:28.388
-I would never sit
across from him.

00:01:28.388 --> 00:01:30.156
-You would never?
You wouldn't talk to him?

00:01:30.156 --> 00:01:31.224
-No.

00:01:31.224 --> 00:01:32.958
I'd sit across from Barack,
though.

00:01:32.958 --> 00:01:34.094
-Oh.

00:01:34.094 --> 00:01:35.761
Donald Trump
isn't an at-risk youth,

00:01:35.761 --> 00:01:39.165
but LeBron just took him
to school.

00:01:39.165 --> 00:01:41.834
So Trump decided to soothe
his ego the way he always does

00:01:41.834 --> 00:01:44.037
by surrounding himself
with fawning supporters.

00:01:44.037 --> 00:01:46.338
On Saturday, he flew to Ohio

00:01:46.338 --> 00:01:48.040
to campaign for a local
Republican Congressman

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:49.742
and concocted a fantasy

00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:52.645
about winning the women's vote
in the 2016 election,

00:01:52.645 --> 00:01:54.681
which he actually lost
by 12 points.

00:01:54.681 --> 00:01:57.049
-I won the women.
I won the women.

00:01:57.049 --> 00:01:58.317
Oh.

00:01:58.317 --> 00:02:00.319
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:00.319 --> 00:02:02.321
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:02.321 --> 00:02:05.791
You know, when those numbers
came, how is it possible?

00:02:05.791 --> 00:02:08.194
Because I never heard
I was going to win the women.

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:10.930
I said,
"I think the women like me."

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:13.132
My wife, the First Lady,
Melania, said,

00:02:13.132 --> 00:02:16.135
"The women really like you."

00:02:16.135 --> 00:02:19.238
They do like me.
And I like them.

00:02:19.238 --> 00:02:21.307
But I said,
"How did we win the women?"

00:02:21.307 --> 00:02:22.742
We won the women.

00:02:22.742 --> 00:02:24.010
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:25.645
-Is it me
or he is starting to sound

00:02:25.645 --> 00:02:27.347
like late-stage Jerry Lewis?

00:02:27.347 --> 00:02:29.716
How did we win the women?
We won the women.

00:02:29.716 --> 00:02:32.151
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.151 --> 00:02:34.386
That's right.
Trump says he won the women.

00:02:34.386 --> 00:02:36.522
And we only had to pay off
some of them.

00:02:36.522 --> 00:02:37.557
[ Audience "Ohs" ]

00:02:37.557 --> 00:02:38.658
I love --

00:02:38.658 --> 00:02:39.759
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:39.759 --> 00:02:42.995
I love how obviously fake
this story is.

00:02:42.995 --> 00:02:45.030
But this is the part
that really gives it away.

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:47.333
My wife, the First Lady,
Melania, said,

00:02:47.333 --> 00:02:48.835
"The women really like you."

00:02:48.835 --> 00:02:51.136
-Can't you just see Melania
on election night

00:02:51.136 --> 00:02:54.307
poring over the exit polls
with a green eye shade on?

00:02:54.307 --> 00:02:56.375
"Darling,
the women really like you,

00:02:56.375 --> 00:02:59.946
especially white women
age 80 to 110."

00:02:59.946 --> 00:03:01.447
[ Laughter ]

00:03:01.447 --> 00:03:03.349
Trump wants us to think
his wife talks to him.

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:04.717
Look at her.

00:03:04.717 --> 00:03:07.753
Her body may be there,
but her mind is on Amazon Prime

00:03:07.753 --> 00:03:09.555
shopping for a LeBron Jersey.

00:03:09.555 --> 00:03:11.691
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:11.691 --> 00:03:13.559
You can tell.

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:16.963
You can tell Trump's ego
is really bruised this weekend

00:03:16.963 --> 00:03:20.099
because he ripped through some
of his greatest hits on Saturday

00:03:20.099 --> 00:03:21.934
while adding a few new wrinkles,

00:03:21.934 --> 00:03:24.404
like when he bragged about his
plan to create a Space Force,

00:03:24.404 --> 00:03:28.174
but also seemed to imply that
something was happening on Mars.

00:03:28.174 --> 00:03:31.311
-I've also directed the Pentagon
to begin the process

00:03:31.311 --> 00:03:32.945
of creating the sixth branch

00:03:32.945 --> 00:03:34.947
of the United States
Armed Forces

00:03:34.947 --> 00:03:37.050
called the Space Force.

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:38.117
Space.

00:03:38.117 --> 00:03:39.619
Very important.

00:03:39.619 --> 00:03:41.654
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:45.057 --> 00:03:46.359
That's going to be great.

00:03:46.359 --> 00:03:47.994
Look, so much is happening now
in space.

00:03:47.994 --> 00:03:49.128
I mean, your great defense.

00:03:49.128 --> 00:03:51.063
I'm not just talking
about Mars and the moon,

00:03:51.063 --> 00:03:54.500
I'm talking about tremendous
defense capability.

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:56.836
-What does he think is happening
on Mars?

00:03:56.836 --> 00:03:58.103
[ Laughter ]

00:03:58.103 --> 00:03:59.706
[ As Trump ]
Mars is a great place.

00:03:59.706 --> 00:04:00.906
I've been there many times.

00:04:00.906 --> 00:04:02.841
In fact, it's red because
they voted for me.

00:04:02.841 --> 00:04:04.476
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:04.476 --> 00:04:07.079
We -- We won the Martians.

00:04:07.079 --> 00:04:08.881
They said we'd never win
the Martians,

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:10.883
but we won the Martians.

00:04:10.883 --> 00:04:12.585
My wife, First Lady Melania,
she says,

00:04:12.585 --> 00:04:14.320
"I think these Martians
really like you."

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:16.155
[ Laughter ]

00:04:16.155 --> 00:04:17.690
[ Normal voice ]
But it wouldn't be a Trump rally

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:19.192
without a bizarre rant
about how popular he is.

00:04:19.192 --> 00:04:22.795
This time, he was bragging about
taking down a GOP Congressman

00:04:22.795 --> 00:04:24.630
who is critical of him,
Mark Sanford,

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:26.899
after supporting
Sanford's opponent in a primary.

00:04:26.899 --> 00:04:29.602
Now, when Sanford was governor
in 2009,

00:04:29.602 --> 00:04:32.071
he famously had an affair
with a woman in Argentina

00:04:32.071 --> 00:04:35.340
and told his wife he was hiking
the Appalachian Trail.

00:04:35.340 --> 00:04:37.176
Trump has brought this up
before,

00:04:37.176 --> 00:04:40.045
but he keeps getting the name
of the Appalachian Trail wrong.

00:04:40.045 --> 00:04:42.781
-Katie Arrington,
South Carolina.

00:04:42.781 --> 00:04:44.817
She was behind by a lot,

00:04:44.817 --> 00:04:47.620
and she is fantastic,
by the way.

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:48.754
She's fantastic.

00:04:48.754 --> 00:04:50.723
And we endorsed her,

00:04:50.723 --> 00:04:54.960
and she beat a man that likes
flamingo dancers from Argentina.

00:04:54.960 --> 00:04:56.529
You know about that.

00:04:58.864 --> 00:05:02.935
He was supposed
to be vacationing

00:05:02.935 --> 00:05:06.539
on the Tallahassee trail, but
he was actually in Argentina.

00:05:06.539 --> 00:05:08.040
[ Laughter ]

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:09.408
I don't know.

00:05:09.408 --> 00:05:11.977
Jim, do they have a Tallahassee
trail in Argentina?

00:05:11.977 --> 00:05:13.446
I don't think, right?

00:05:13.446 --> 00:05:16.282
-No, they don't, and they don't
have one in America either.

00:05:16.282 --> 00:05:17.850
[ Laughter ]

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:20.285
Tallahassee trail
sounds like a cheap rip-off

00:05:20.285 --> 00:05:22.287
of "The Oregon Trail."

00:05:22.287 --> 00:05:25.725
The year is 2018, and you must
survive the treacherous journey

00:05:25.725 --> 00:05:29.529
from Tallahassee to your private
golf course in New Jersey.

00:05:29.529 --> 00:05:32.498
Your only supplies are a private
jet and a bucket of KFC.

00:05:32.498 --> 00:05:34.033
And uh-oh!
You have dementia.

00:05:34.033 --> 00:05:37.069
[ Laughter ]

00:05:37.069 --> 00:05:38.204
Also --

00:05:38.204 --> 00:05:40.239
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:42.408 --> 00:05:45.411
Can we go back to this part
of the clip for a second?

00:05:45.411 --> 00:05:49.916
-She beat a man that likes
flamingo dancers from Argentina.

00:05:49.916 --> 00:05:52.151
-Flamingo dancers?

00:05:52.151 --> 00:05:54.987
Do you mean flamenco dancers?

00:05:54.987 --> 00:05:56.488
[ As Trump ] Everyone knows
the famous

00:05:56.488 --> 00:05:58.658
dancing flamingos of Argentina.

00:05:58.658 --> 00:06:00.760
[ Laughter ]

00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:02.661
Of course,
Trump would rather everyone talk

00:06:02.661 --> 00:06:05.031
about his attacks on LeBron
or the Space Force

00:06:05.031 --> 00:06:06.332
and his mounting legal problems,

00:06:06.332 --> 00:06:07.800
which are getting worse
by the day

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:09.368
as more information comes out

00:06:09.368 --> 00:06:10.903
about that infamous
Trump Tower meeting

00:06:10.903 --> 00:06:12.538
with the Russians in 2016.

00:06:12.538 --> 00:06:15.140
Now remember, when we first
learned about that meeting,

00:06:15.140 --> 00:06:17.176
the president's son, Don Jr.,
insisted

00:06:17.176 --> 00:06:18.777
that his father wasn't there.

00:06:18.777 --> 00:06:20.779
He also claimed
the meeting was about a law

00:06:20.779 --> 00:06:24.016
sanctioning Russian officials
called the Magnitsky Act,

00:06:24.016 --> 00:06:26.118
as well as Russia's response
to that law which,

00:06:26.118 --> 00:06:29.054
was to ban Americans
from adopting Russian children.

00:06:29.054 --> 00:06:31.924
-The pretext of the meeting was,
"Hey, we have information,"

00:06:31.924 --> 00:06:32.958
and there was,
you know, some small talk.

00:06:32.958 --> 00:06:34.827
I don't even know what it was.

00:06:34.827 --> 00:06:37.496
It just was sort of nonsensical,
inane, and garbled,

00:06:37.496 --> 00:06:39.798
and then quickly went on to,
you know,

00:06:39.798 --> 00:06:42.435
a story about Russian adoption
and how we could possibly help.

00:06:42.435 --> 00:06:43.969
And really,
that's where we shut it down,

00:06:43.969 --> 00:06:45.438
which is, "Wait a second.

00:06:45.438 --> 00:06:47.240
What does this have to do with
what we were talking about?"

00:06:47.240 --> 00:06:49.875
-Did you even know
what Magnitsky Act was?

00:06:49.875 --> 00:06:52.111
-I'd never even heard of it
before, you know, that day.

00:06:52.111 --> 00:06:54.447
-So his defense
against Russian collusion

00:06:54.447 --> 00:06:56.716
is that he's an idiot
who's also a bad person.

00:06:56.716 --> 00:06:57.916
[ Light laughter ]

00:06:57.916 --> 00:06:59.519
Did you know
what the Magnitsky Act was?

00:06:59.519 --> 00:07:01.120
I had no idea, and as soon as
they started

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:04.590
talking about helping orphans,
we shut it down.

00:07:04.590 --> 00:07:06.592
Also, can we go back to this
for a second?

00:07:06.592 --> 00:07:08.394
-There was, you know,
some small talk.

00:07:08.394 --> 00:07:10.029
I don't even remember
what it was.

00:07:10.029 --> 00:07:12.331
It just was sort of nonsensical,
inane, and garbled.

00:07:12.331 --> 00:07:14.266
-"Nonsensical, inane,
and garbled."

00:07:14.266 --> 00:07:16.102
So your father was there!

00:07:16.102 --> 00:07:18.571
[ Laughter ]

00:07:18.571 --> 00:07:20.573
A dead giveaway.

00:07:20.573 --> 00:07:21.874
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:21.874 --> 00:07:25.044
It was nonsensical, inane,
and garbled.

00:07:25.044 --> 00:07:28.480
It was something about dancing
flamingos on Mars.

00:07:28.480 --> 00:07:29.582
So there you go.
That was their story.

00:07:29.582 --> 00:07:30.750
It was about adoptions,

00:07:30.750 --> 00:07:32.118
not about getting dirt
on Hillary Clinton.

00:07:32.118 --> 00:07:33.585
At least that was their story
until yesterday,

00:07:33.585 --> 00:07:34.686
when Trump, in an effort

00:07:34.686 --> 00:07:36.288
to distance himself
from the meeting,

00:07:36.288 --> 00:07:39.591
tweeted that he wasn't there,
and admitted its real purpose.

00:07:39.591 --> 00:07:40.960
-Here's a
tweet that he sent out.

00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:42.061
He writes...

00:07:58.043 --> 00:07:59.545
-He's so bad at this.

00:07:59.545 --> 00:08:01.080
[ Laughter ]

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:02.415
[ As Trump ]
You guys, it's totally legal,

00:08:02.415 --> 00:08:03.716
and I didn't know
anything about it.

00:08:03.716 --> 00:08:06.118
Ask anyone that was hiking
the Tallahassee trail!

00:08:06.118 --> 00:08:07.720
[ Laughter ]

00:08:07.720 --> 00:08:09.722
[ Normal voice ] So now --
Now that the president

00:08:09.722 --> 00:08:12.658
has admitted that he and his son
lied repeatedly

00:08:12.658 --> 00:08:14.759
and that the meeting actually
was about colluding

00:08:14.759 --> 00:08:15.961
with a foreign adversary,

00:08:15.961 --> 00:08:17.930
Trump's lawyers are trying
a new argument

00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:20.799
that even if he did collude,
it's not a crime.

00:08:20.799 --> 00:08:22.735
-Trump wrote on Twitter...

00:08:29.775 --> 00:08:31.977
-I've been sitting here looking
in the Federal Code

00:08:31.977 --> 00:08:33.613
trying to find collusion
as a crime.

00:08:33.613 --> 00:08:35.948
-It's not.
-Collusion is not a crime.

00:08:35.948 --> 00:08:37.549
-This was a meeting
to get information

00:08:37.549 --> 00:08:39.184
from the Crown Prosecutor
of Russia

00:08:39.184 --> 00:08:41.353
on Hillary Clinton's campaign.

00:08:41.353 --> 00:08:44.123
How would that be legal?

00:08:44.123 --> 00:08:46.092
-Well, the question is
how would it be illegal?

00:08:46.092 --> 00:08:48.260
-How would it be illegal?
I don't know.

00:08:48.260 --> 00:08:50.462
How about a conspiracy
to violate election laws

00:08:50.462 --> 00:08:52.464
or conspiracy to defraud
the United States?

00:08:52.464 --> 00:08:55.668
Seriously, how is it possible
that these are the best lawyers

00:08:55.668 --> 00:08:58.170
the President
of the United States can get?

00:08:58.170 --> 00:09:00.205
They're like
personal injury lawyers

00:09:00.205 --> 00:09:04.143
in that they're lawyers who
personally injure their client.

00:09:04.143 --> 00:09:05.878
Rudy Giuliani
is the kind of lawyer

00:09:05.878 --> 00:09:08.280
who would spend all day
chasing an ambulance

00:09:08.280 --> 00:09:10.482
only to realize
it was an ice cream truck.

00:09:10.482 --> 00:09:12.084
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:12.084 --> 00:09:14.987
And then today,
there were major developments

00:09:14.987 --> 00:09:17.222
in the trial of Trump's
ex-campaign chairman

00:09:17.222 --> 00:09:18.523
Paul Manafort.

00:09:18.523 --> 00:09:20.426
Manafort's business partner
Rick Gates,

00:09:20.426 --> 00:09:23.095
who was also Trump's
deputy campaign chairman,

00:09:23.095 --> 00:09:24.964
testified against Manafort.

00:09:24.964 --> 00:09:27.700
And here is the real transcript
from Gates' testimony.

00:09:35.274 --> 00:09:36.475
Oh, my God.

00:09:36.475 --> 00:09:38.144
This whole thing is like
a "Law &amp; Order" episode

00:09:38.144 --> 00:09:41.046
that ends in first five minutes.

00:09:41.046 --> 00:09:43.615
"Did you do crimes?"
"Yes. I did crimes."

00:09:43.615 --> 00:09:45.183 line:0%
♪♪

00:09:45.183 --> 00:09:46.785 line:0%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:46.785 --> 00:09:48.320 line:0%
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:09:48.320 --> 00:09:50.089 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:50.089 --> 00:09:51.891 line:0%
♪♪

